  Warning                                                         2600 1451   41
 =================================================================2600 1451   42
  MF/MT combinations used to define photoionization subshell cross2600 1451   43
  sections (MF=23, MT=534-572) and coherent anomalous scattering  2600 1451   44
  factors (MF=27, MT=505 AND 506) are newly defined MF/MT numbers 2600 1451   45
  for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist in earlier versions of ENDF/B. 2600 1451   46
  If you are not prepared to use this data you need merely delete 2600 1451   47
  it and all of the remaining data will still be consistent and   2600 1451   48
  equivalent to the types of data in earlier versions of ENDF/B.  2600 1451   49
  However, this will limit the range of problems to which this    2600 1451   50
  data can be applied (see: ref. 1 for details).                  2600 1451   51
 =================================================================2600 1451   52
  Definition of new types of data                                 2600 1451   53
 =================================================================2600 1451   54
  1) The total photoionization cross section is equal to the sum  2600 1451   55
     of the photoionization subshell cross sections.              2600 1451   56
                                                                  2600 1451   57
     For each subshell on the second line of a section the C1 and 2600 1451   58
     C2 fields are defined as,                                    2600 1451   59
                                                                  2600 1451   60
     EPE = The photoionization edge energy (similar to Q-value)   2600 1451   61
     EFL = The fluorescence yield (eV/photoionization)            2600 1451   62
                                                                  2600 1451   63
  2) The angular distribution of coherently scattered photons is, 2600 1451   64
                                                                  2600 1451   65
     S(E,MU) = 3*T/8*(1 + MU**2)*((FF(M)+F1(E))**2+(F2(E))**2)    2600 1451   66
                                                                  2600 1451   67
     S(E,MU) = Angular distributions (barns per unit cosine)      2600 1451   68
     T       = The Thomson cross section                          2600 1451   69
     MU      = The cosine of the scattering angle                 2600 1451   70
     FF(M)   = The atomic form factor                             2600 1451   71
     M       = Momentum transfer = SIN(THETA/2)/LAMBDA/4*PI       2600 1451   72
     F1(E)   = The real anomalous scattering factor               2600 1451   73
     F2(E)   = The imaginary anomalous scattering factor          2600 1451   74
                                                                  2600 1451   75
     F1(E) and F2(E) are isotropic.                               2600 1451   76
                                                                  2600 1451   77
     When F1(E) = F2(E) = 0 this reduces to the result obtained   2600 1451   78
     using only form factors (the older ENDF/B convention).       2600 1451   79
 =================================================================2600 1451   80
 Differences between EPDL97 and the data base presented here      2600 1451   81
 =================================================================2600 1451   82
 1) Energy range - EPDL97 - 1 eV to 100 GeV                       2600 1451   83
                   Here   - 1 eV TO 100 GeV (previously 100 MeV)  2600 1451   84
 2) Type of Data - EPDL97 - Photon interaction including          2600 1451   85
                            photoexcitation                       2600 1451   86
                   Here   - Photon interaction  - ENDF/B-VI has   2600 1451   87
                            no provision for photoexcitation      2600 1451   88
 3) Secondary E  - EPDL97 - Average energy of each secondary      2600 1451   89
                            (photons, electrons, positrons)       2600 1451   90
                   HERE   - No secondary energy data              2600 1451   91
 4) Interpolation- EPDL97 - Cross sections are Log X vs. Log Y    2600 1451   92
                            interpolable - the total cross        2600 1451   93
                            section is not included               2600 1451   94
                          - Form factors and scattering functions 2600 1451   95
                            are Log X vs. Log y, except first     2600 1451   96
                            interval.                             2600 1451   97
                          - Anomalous scattering factors linearly 2600 1451   98
                            interpolable (they can be negative)   2600 1451   99
                   Here   - Up through ENDF/B-V photon interaction2600 1451  100
                            cross sections were Log X vs. Log Y.  2600 1451  101
                          - For the first two Mods. of ENDF/B-VI  2600 1451  102
                            in order to consistently define the   2600 1451  103
                            total cross sections at ALL energies  2600 1451  104
                            all cross sections were linearized.   2600 1451  105
                            This was NOT a good idea.             2600 1451  106
                          - Starting with Mod. 3, cross sections  2600 1451  107
                            are left in Log X vs. Log. Y form so  2600 1451  108
                            that they are IDENTICAL to what's in  2600 1451  109
                            EPDL97.                               2600 1451  110
                            The total is defined ONLY at the      2600 1451  111
                            energies tabulated in any other cross 2600 1451  112
                            section.                              2600 1451  113
                 WARNING  - As a result the total cross section   2600 1451  114
                            MUST NOT be interpolated to define the2600 1451  115
                            total between tabulated energies. The 2600 1451  116
                            ONLY consist way to define the total  2600 1451  117
                            between tabulated energies is to      2600 1451  118
                            interpolate all of the partials and   2600 1451  119
                            add them up.                          2600 1451  120
